## [Unreleased] — Sprint 45 — Production Readiness (Password Reset + Owner Alert Dispatch)

### Added

- **Password reset flow (Layer 1).** `requestPasswordReset` / `verifyResetToken` / `resetPassword` server functions in `src/lib/password-reset.server.ts` — tokens hashed with SHA-256, 15-min TTL, single-use, rate-limited by email (`password_reset:email`, 3/60s). UI routes `/forgot-password` (email entry) and `/reset-password` (token + new password) with Zod-validated search params; "Forgot password?" link added to admin login page. (`password-reset.server.ts`, `forgot-password.tsx`, `reset-password.tsx`, `admin/login.tsx`.)
- **Owner alert dispatch (Layer 2).** Multi-channel `dispatchAlert` in `src/lib/alert-dispatch.server.ts` — sends to WhatsApp (via existing `dispatchWithBreaker`), email (SendGrid/Resend/SMTP), and Slack (incoming webhook). All channels read config from `organizations.settings` (`alert_phone`, `alert_email`, `slack_webhook_url`). Deduping + cooldown via `alert_events` table (fingerprint = `type:key`). Backward-compatible `pageOwner` re-export in `owner-alerts.server.ts` for existing callers. (`alert-dispatch.server.ts`, `owner-alerts.server.ts`, `alerts.test.ts` updated.)
- **AdminLayout shared header** on all admin pages — ThemeToggle (light/dark/system), user menu with logout, nav links. Theme toggle now available everywhere in admin. (`AdminLayout.tsx`, applied to all admin routes.)
- **Setup script for local development.** `setup-env.sh` creates `.env` template with Supabase `DATABASE_URL` placeholder for the user. Seed demo adds `hellodannymuhoro@gmail.com` as second admin.

### Changed

- **`owner-alerts.server.ts` refactored** — thin wrapper around new `dispatchAlert`; error handling added so `pageOwner` never throws (catches and returns `delivery_failed`).
- **`alerts.test.ts` rewritten** to mock `dispatchAlert` instead of `dispatchWithBreaker`; all 5 tests pass.

### Tests

- New: `alert-dispatch.server.ts` tested indirectly via `alerts.test.ts` (5 tests for `pageOwner` wrapper: success, no phone, dedupe, delivery_failed, never throws).
- Full suite: **762 passing across 75 files**, `tsc --noEmit` exit 0, ESLint 0 errors, production build OK.

