## [Unreleased] — Sprint 41 — Tier 4 Release Polish (Doc Accuracy + Public Contact Intake)

### Added

- **Public "Send us a message" intake writes a real tenant-scoped lead.**
  `src/lib/api/contact.server.ts` adds `submitContactMessage` (POST, Zod-validated) delegating to
  the exported `ingestContactMessage` core. Anonymous visitors no longer need a session cookie: the
  handler resolves the public org by slug (`PUBLIC_ORG_SLUG`, default `kays-wellness`), **fails
  closed** when the org row is missing (`unavailable`, no write), rate-limits per email
  (`contact:<email>`, 5/60s), encrypts `name`/`email` via `encryptFields` (ADR-015), and inserts a
  pipeline-ready lead (`status='new'`, `channel='web_form'`, `service='Contact Message'` with the
  message body in `raw_payload`) — plus a `lead_interactions` `new` row, a `lead:acquired` SSE
  publish, a `LEAD_INGESTED` audit entry, and the staff notification enqueue. The `src/routes/
  contact.tsx` form now drives it through `useMutation` and surfaces every result (created /
  rate_limited / unavailable / db_unavailable); failures never silently drop the message or clear
  the form.
- **`docs/current-state.md`** — the orientation doc AGENTS.md rule 6 required: run/verify commands,
  the public lead-path reality, security posture, and the ASPIRATIONAL capability list.

### Changed

- **`docs/architecture.md` gaps table brought current.** The two stale rows (no CI pipeline, no
  login rate limiting) are now marked Resolved with citations (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`;
  `auth.server.ts:114`); the four still-true gaps are kept with `file:line` evidence; the header,
  CI/CD row, `registration.server.ts` one-liner, and test totals (730/69 → 743/70) were refreshed.
- **`docs/db-contracts.md`** tracks the new anonymous writer (`api/contact.server.ts` on
  `clinic_leads` + `lead_interactions`) and documents the public-intake tenant-resolution contract
  (AGENTS rule 2).

### Tests

- `src/__tests__/contact-message.test.ts` (13 tests) — schema rules; real-core write-path proofs
  (INSERT bound to the resolved org, encrypted PII, plaintext absent, message in `raw_payload`);
  fail-closed proofs (missing org → one query + zero INSERTs, DB down → `getDb` never called,
  rate limit → INSERT never fired); side-effect assertions.
- Full suite: **743 passing across 70 files**, `tsc --noEmit` exit 0, ESLint 0 errors on touched
  files, production build OK, Playwright E2E 5/5.

