## [Unreleased] — Pilot Hardening (v1.1.0-pilot) — Sprint 38

### Added

- **Production database connected.** Root cause of the long-standing blocker: the Supabase direct
  host is IPv6-only and unreachable from Vercel; the correct route is the **transaction pooler**
  `aws-1-eu-west-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543` (the CLI's linked project revealed `aws-1`, not
  `aws-0`). The owner's new password authenticates. Connection string verified through the app's
  own `postgres` driver.
- **All 12 Vercel env vars set** (DATABASE_URL, SESSION_SECRET, NODE_ENV, admin creds, M-Pesa
  sandbox vars) across production/preview/development.
- **Org + admin seeded in production Supabase** — org "Kay's Wellness Centre" (`kays-wellness`),
  admin `admin@kayswellnesscentre.org`, default Mon–Sat availability. **Login verified end-to-end**
  via the production `/_serverFn/*` RPC (200, `set-cookie`, role admin). All 28 tenant tables
  created.
- **WhatsApp delivery enabled with real credentials.** `WHATSAPP_TOKEN` + `WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID`
  set in all three Vercel environments (raise: 14 vars total). Live test send to a real Kenya number
  delivered (`wamid.HBgMMjU0NzAzOTM5MjM2FQIAERgSRjlFMURDRjhFQTk2MEEyNDI1AA==`). Token A is
  short-lived (expires 2026-08-27T17:00:00 UTC); converting to a permanent system-user token is an
  owner follow-up.
- **M-Pesa STK push from a paid invoice.** Billing ledger rows for unpaid/issued invoices carry an
  emerald "M-Pesa" button that opens an STK prompt modal (phone pre-filled from the decrypted
  `lead_phone`, account reference derived from the invoice number) and sends the push via
  `initiateStkPush`. Server-side STK (sandbox `ResponseCode: 0`) validated under
  `mpesa-stk-push.test.ts`; the UI trigger is covered by a new happy-dom render test.
- **Circuit breaker on the live dispatch path.** `dispatchWithBreaker` wraps `sendWithFallback`
  (WhatsApp primary, honest SMS = no fake adapter) so `dispatchLeadMessage` and the queue worker's
  `dispatchNotification` both fail closed when all channels are circuit-open, and report real
  delivery status instead of claiming a fallback that doesn't exist.
- **Message ledger audit trail.** Every outbound WhatsApp dispatch now writes an `outbound` row via
  `logMessage` (status `sent`/`failed`, provider + event metadata); ledger failures are logged and
  never break the dispatch.

### Fixed

- **"Invalid lazy handler" 500 on every `/api/*` route.** Nitro 3 beta's Vercel web-format lazy
  handler resolves only a module's **default export**; our route files exported named `GET`/`POST`
  only. Added default method-dispatch exports to all 6 API route handlers. Verified: health → 200,
  mpesa GET → 405, whatsapp GET → 403.
- **"Cannot find package 'postgres'" on every DB access.** `db.server.ts` imported postgres via an
  obfuscated dynamic import that hid the specifier from the server bundler too, leaving it
  externalized in the serverless bundle. Switched to a literal `import("postgres")` + client-env
  rollup external. `/api/health` now returns `{"status":"healthy","dbAvailable":true}` from the
  deployed function.
- **`/api/health` reports real connectivity.** Added `pingDb()` (runs `SELECT 1`, updates state);
  the endpoint no longer reads a passive flag that only turned true after any DB query.
- **Stock Unsplash photos still diverged from Lovable.** Copy and theme matched, but home, our-story
  and resources rendered generic Unsplash stock photos while Lovable served the clinic's own branded
  imagery. Wired the repo's local `src/assets` images (byte-identical to Lovable's, MD5-verified) into
  every component: `hero-clinic.jpg` (home hero + carousel), `dr-jackie.jpg` (home + our-story),
  `team-1/2/3.jpg` (our-story), `wellness-1/2/3.jpg` (resources). The hero carousel now renders light
  text on the plain page background (matching Lovable) instead of overlaying text on a dark photo.
  og:image/twitter:image now point to the stable `https://kays-wellness-centre.vercel.app/og/hero-clinic.jpg`
  instead of an Unsplash URL. Built asset hashes now match Lovable's exactly
  (`hero-clinic-CjGQtwC_.jpg`, `dr-jackie-BPEGanEG.jpg`, `team-1-BpnzEXNC.jpg`, `wellness-1-CgFIaApR.jpg`).
- **Elite "Warm Midnight Forest" dark theme.** The dark mode was the generic dark-green palette the
  site shipped with (Lovable has no dark mode, so it was designed from scratch). New warm
  charcoal-forest ground carries the brand's savannah-olive DNA with a luminous sage-olive primary,
  burnished terracotta ember accent and warm gold highlights. Added `color-scheme` (light/dark),
  theme-aware glass border, dark `text-gradient`, slim on-theme scrollbars, accent selection,
  premium focus ring, and a smooth cross-fade on theme toggle. 40+ `dark:text-*-400` variants keep
  status colors legible on the dark ground; all hardcoded `gray-*` swapped for theme tokens. Light
  theme verified byte-identical to the Lovable deploy in compiled CSS. Admin Operations Dashboard
  gained an "At a glance." header, live-telemetry indicator and card-lift hover.

### Changed

- **Vercel UI now matches the Lovable deploy.** Two causes fixed permanently: (1) theme defaulted
  to the OS color-scheme (dark systems rendered the whole site dark) — now defaults to light,
  matching Lovable; (2) home + services copy was the older "Premium Functional Medicine / Nairobi"
  version — aligned to Lovable's "Holistic Medical Care in Kenya": hero slides (Root-Cause
  Medicine, Whole-Person Care, Global Mission), Our Focus (4 areas), Global Mission section,
  Start Your Journey, and the "From firefighting illness to true wellness" CTA. Services page now
  shows Specialized Treatments (4 conditions), Functional Medicine Delivered, and Clinic Offerings.
  Removed the Specialty-modal grid from home. Updated titles/OG/Twitter meta.

### Verified

- `/api/health` → healthy (DB connected) in production.
- All 6 API routes functional in production.
- Org + admin login verified in production.
- Vercel home + services render the Lovable copy with no dark class in SSR.
- Vercel home, our-story and resources serve the branded local images (no Unsplash refs); built
  asset hashes are byte-identical to Lovable's. Live production (deploy `dpl_2eWDgruP43Uimh9Btb2KnRpeQRng`)
  serves the images byte-identical (MD5-verified over HTTPS) and `/api/health` is healthy.
- Light theme byte-identical to Lovable in compiled CSS; new dark palette + `dark:text-*-400` rules
  confirmed in compiled output; SSR home renders light by default.
- WhatsApp live send delivered with real credentials; 695 tests / 62 files green (incl. new
  STK UI render test + breaker/ledger wiring tests), tsc exit 0, eslint 0 errors, build passes.

### Notes

- The `/_serverFn/*` RPC requires TanStack's seroval cross-JSON payload envelope `{t, f, m}`; a raw
  JSON body is not parseable by the server deserializer (framework behavior, not a bug).

### Docs

- `docs/sprints/sprint-38-production-golive-api-fixes-ui-parity.md`: full sprint record (Tier 1:
  WhatsApp env + STK trigger + circuit-breaker dispatch + message ledger in Part 7).
- `docs/sprints/sprint-37-production-webhook-fix-deployment.md`: superseded (blockers now resolved).

